From 10cea38be1b6a70d2dd99af13235c8246095b664 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:03:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Custody v2 panel: seats as the vault counts them, per-call
 book check, SessionVault refusal, agreed-read shape
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per root review (ROOT-REVIEW-STATUS.txt):
- describeCommittee counts seats as custody/v2/protocol.mjs seatLayout does: all Enclave-flagged machines form ONE seat.
  SINGLE-SEAT BOOTSTRAP is used only when n = 1 (production: n 1, t 1, W 1). More seats are stated exactly, with no claim
  of independent operators or failure domains.
- Only the vault's code identity is cached per page. The book's secretVaultV2 is re-read on every call, so the
  administrator's rollback stops v2 actions at once.
- A deployment held by a SessionVault the vault does not unwrap (the book names no sessionVaultFactory) is refused
  precisely (session_vault_not_unwrapped). It is not mistaken for a Safe/passkey account. Neither routes through ownerCall.
- Fix, found by the real-contract test: the agreed reader merges an OBJECT result with its block facts, so a scalar
  snapshot result was lost (the book check read "[object Object]"). Snapshot callbacks now return objects; the fixture
  vault mimics the real shape.
- The first-policy committee comes from the page config (production: the live 0x4774… genesis constant).
